WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:12.372
Pete sat down at a table in the bookstore with a freshly baked chocolate-chip cookie.

2
00:00:12.373 --> 00:00:16.980
Abdul was already there, waiting for him to start their session.

3
00:00:16.981 --> 00:00:21.234
Pete was tutoring the younger boy, helping him with his English class.

4
00:00:21.235 --> 00:00:27.503
Pete was about to bite into the cookie when he noticed Abdul had only books in front of him today.

5
00:00:27.504 --> 00:00:30.230
"Abdul, aren't you getting a snack?"

6
00:00:30.231 --> 00:00:37.389
Abdul shook his head. "It's Ramadan," he said quietly, "so I'm fasting."

7
00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:42.250
Pete felt his face turn bright red. "Oh, sorry . . . "

8
00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:46.248
Quickly he changed the subject and put down the cookie.

9
00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:49.518
"What do you need to study for your exam?"

10
00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:53.474
Abdul pointed to a handout filled with English words.

11
00:00:53.475 --> 00:00:56.838
He had written their Arabic definitions in the margin.

12
00:00:56.839 --> 00:01:02.229
"I'd like to review this vocabulary, as well as some possible essay questions."

13
00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:06.840
While they reviewed material for Abdul's test, Pete was curious.

14
00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:13.362
He knew Ramadan was the holiest time of year for Muslims, the followers of Islam.

15
00:01:13.363 --> 00:01:22.688
Since Muslims made up nearly a quarter of the world's population, Ramadan was a big holiday in Islamic and even non-Islamic countries.

16
00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:26.504
But that was about all he knew.

17
00:01:26.505 --> 00:01:32.211
When they took a break, Pete asked Abdul to tell him more about Ramadan.

18
00:01:32.212 --> 00:01:42.848
"Ramadan commemorates the time when a prophet named Muhammad received important teachings from Allah—that's the name for God in our religion," Abdul explained.

19
00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:48.589
"Muhammad recorded those teachings in the Qur'an, the holy book of Islam."

20
00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:55.300
As Pete listened to Abdul, his stomach rumbled with hunger—he still hadn't eaten his snack.

21
00:01:55.301 --> 00:01:58.626
"How long is Ramadan?"

22
00:01:58.627 --> 00:02:01.928
"It's one lunar month.

23
00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:10.097
We observe Ramadan during the ninth month of the Islamic calendar, and it begins when the new moon arrives."

24
00:02:10.098 --> 00:02:14.811
"How do you survive while fasting for a whole month?" Pete asked.

25
00:02:14.812 --> 00:02:22.526
Abdul laughed. "We eat a little, but only before sunrise and after sunset.

26
00:02:22.527 --> 00:02:27.938
In fact, the whole month is named Ramadan, which means . . . " He thought for a second.

27
00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:32.055
"'Burning heat.' The burning can mean the burning of fasting.

28
00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:35.804
Or it can mean the burning away of sins by fasting."

29
00:02:35.805 --> 00:02:39.887
"Do all Muslims fast for Ramadan?" Pete asked.

30
00:02:39.888 --> 00:02:44.491
"Sick people and young children don't," Abdul explained.

31
00:02:44.492 --> 00:02:49.490
"I started fasting gradually, for brief periods, when I was around ten years old.

32
00:02:49.491 --> 00:02:53.132
But Ramadan isn't just about fasting.

33
00:02:53.133 --> 00:03:00.736
We also pray more and perform charitable deeds such as helping others or donating food and money. Good

34
00:03:00.737 --> 00:03:05.137
deeds are important to our faith." "It

35
00:03:05.138 --> 00:03:09.400
must be hard to fast for a month," Pete said. Abdul

36
00:03:09.401 --> 00:03:17.075
eyed Pete's tray. "Please, Pete, eat your snack. Fasting

37
00:03:17.076 --> 00:03:23.353
is hard, but I'm used to it. Besides, this is a sacred time for me. During

38
00:03:23.354 --> 00:03:27.196
Ramadan I grow closer to my family and Allah. I

39
00:03:27.197 --> 00:03:30.332
also gain more compassion for those who are suffering. I

40
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:34.988
believe this makes me a stronger person and a better Muslim." Pete

41
00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:43.243
nodded and took a few bites of the cookie before quietly wrapping it in a napkin and slipping it into his backpack. "You

42
00:03:43.244 --> 00:03:47.022
seem very curious about Ramadan," Abdul said. "Would

43
00:03:47.023 --> 00:03:51.135
you like to join my family for our iftar tomorrow night? That's

44
00:03:51.136 --> 00:03:53.920
the meal we eat after sunset." "I'd

45
00:03:53.921 --> 00:03:56.586
love to come," Pete said. "Great,"

46
00:03:56.587 --> 00:03:59.424
Abdul said with a smile. "In

47
00:03:59.425 --> 00:04:02.943
the meantime we'd better get back to studying. I

48
00:04:02.944 --> 00:04:07.484
want to do well on my exam." After

49
00:04:07.485 --> 00:04:14.557
dark the next evening, Pete knocked on Abdul's door. "Welcome,

50
00:04:14.558 --> 00:04:18.181
Pete!" Abdul said. He

51
00:04:18.182 --> 00:04:22.825
gestured toward a mat where the family kept their shoes. Pete

52
00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:27.559
slipped off his shoes and then turned to greet Abdul's parents. "Thank

53
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.690
you for inviting me." Abdul's

54
00:04:30.691 --> 00:04:35.584
father shook Pete's hand. "Thank you for coming, Pete." "It

55
00:04:35.585 --> 00:04:43.308
is our pleasure to share our iftar with you," Abdul's mother said, smiling warmly. Soon

56
00:04:43.309 --> 00:04:48.018
Abdul's mother was bringing out platters of food. Pete

57
00:04:48.019 --> 00:04:55.868
followed the family's lead by eating very slowly at first, taking just a date and a few sips of water. Then

58
00:04:55.869 --> 00:05:05.706
he helped himself to some delicious-looking meat kebabs, vegetable salad, and yogurt. "We

59
00:05:05.707 --> 00:05:09.928
will get up before dawn and eat another meal," Abdul said. "That

60
00:05:09.929 --> 00:05:13.021
one is called sahoor ."

61
00:05:13.022 --> 00:05:16.538
"When does Ramadan end?" Pete asked.

62
00:05:16.539 --> 00:05:21.050
"Ramadan ends when the next new moon arrives," Abdul replied.

63
00:05:21.051 --> 00:05:26.621
"And when Ramadan is over, we break our fast with a three-day holiday—Eid al-Fitr.

64
00:05:26.622 --> 00:05:32.016
During Eid al-Fitr, we eat many delicious foods and gather together to pray."

65
00:05:32.017 --> 00:05:35.374
Just then Abdul's grandfather entered the room.

66
00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:39.248
His eyes lit up when Abdul introduced Pete as his tutor.

67
00:05:39.249 --> 00:05:44.474
"So you are the famous Pete! You are doing a great job as Abdul's tutor.

68
00:05:44.475 --> 00:05:47.478
Thank you for teaching him so well."

69
00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:53.214
"Abdul is a very good student," Pete said, "but he's also an excellent teacher.

70
00:05:53.215 --> 00:05:59.532
Thanks to him, I've learned all about Ramadan!"

